WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.671
I wanted to understand performance through the creative itself.

00:00:04.521 --> 00:00:09.220
So I built a dashboard that made each ad playable, with the relevant signals beside it.

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:14.678
I added contextual explanations, so the system could teach while I worked.

00:00:15.528 --> 00:00:19.134
Each signal could lead to a testable creative recommendation.

00:00:19.984 --> 00:00:24.601
I shared the approach with teammates in video and design, and kept refining it.

00:00:25.451 --> 00:00:30.071
Then I connected the recommendations to campaign concepts and structured creative briefs.

00:00:30.921 --> 00:00:39.977
Those briefs could feed an AI-assisted production workflow, with organized footage, brand rules, required formats, and human review.

00:00:40.827 --> 00:00:46.300
The result was a connected learning loop, from performance signal to production-ready creative.

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:56.437
I did not build a dashboard just to report what happened. I built a system to help people understand what happened, decide what to test, and make the next piece of creative.
